        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Let&#x27;s consider the following expression:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Let's consider the following expression:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5 + 3 \\times 7]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 5 + 3 \\times 7]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Notice that this expression contains addition <em>and</em> multiplication. So how do we compute its value?</p>",
            "readable_text": "Notice that this expression contains addition and multiplication. So how do we compute its value?",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To help us, we have the following rule: </p>",
            "readable_text": "To help us, we have the following rule:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<blockquote><p><em>When an expression contains only multiplication and addition (or subtraction), the multiplication should always be carried out first</em>.</p></blockquote>",
            "readable_text": "> When an expression contains only multiplication and addition (or subtraction), the multiplication should always be carried out first.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>So, we must first carry out the multiplication <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (3\\times 7).]</span> We can emphasize this using parentheses <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (\\phantom{0}){:}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "So, we must first carry out the multiplication [MATH: (3\\times 7).] We can emphasize this using parentheses [MATH: (\\phantom{0}){:}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5 + \\big({\\color{blue}3 \\times 7}\\big)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 5 + \\big({\\color{blue}3 \\times 7}\\big)]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Here, the parentheses tell us which part of the expression to do first.</p>",
            "readable_text": "Here, the parentheses tell us which part of the expression to do first.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Now, we evaluate our expression as follows:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5 + (3 \u00d7 7)|=; 5 + 21|=; 26]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Now, we evaluate our expression as follows:\n[MATH: 5 + (3 \u00d7 7)|=; 5 + 21|=; 26]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><strong>Watch out!</strong> If we carried out the operations in a different order, we&#x27;d obtain an <em>incorrect answer!</em></p>",
            "readable_text": "Watch out! If we carried out the operations in a different order, we'd obtain an incorrect answer!",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example, if we perform the addition first, we get</p>",
            "readable_text": "For example, if we perform the addition first, we get",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (5 + 3) \u00d7 7|=; 8 \u00d7 7|=; 56|\u00d7]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: (5 + 3) \u00d7 7|=; 8 \u00d7 7|=; 56|\u00d7]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>which is <em>incorrect!</em></p>",
            "readable_text": "which is incorrect!",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nLet's consider the following expression:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 5 + 3 \\times 7]\n\nContent:\nNotice that this expression contains addition and multiplication. So how do we compute its value?\n\nContent:\nTo help us, we have the following rule:\n\nContent:\n> When an expression contains only multiplication and addition (or subtraction), the multiplication should always be carried out first.\n\nContent:\nSo, we must first carry out the multiplication [MATH: (3\\times 7).] We can emphasize this using parentheses [MATH: (\\phantom{0}){:}]\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 5 + \\big({\\color{blue}3 \\times 7}\\big)]\n\nContent:\nHere, the parentheses tell us which part of the expression to do first.\n\nContent:\nNow, we evaluate our expression as follows:\n[MATH: 5 + (3 \u00d7 7)|=; 5 + 21|=; 26]\n\nContent:\nWatch out! If we carried out the operations in a different order, we'd obtain an incorrect answer!\n\nContent:\nFor example, if we perform the addition first, we get\n\nContent:\n[MATH: (5 + 3) \u00d7 7|=; 8 \u00d7 7|=; 56|\u00d7]\n\nContent:\nwhich is incorrect!"
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 2,
        "step_index": 2,
        "item_type": "step",
        "step_type": "example",
        "step_id": "54306",
        "content_id": "12842",
        "dom_id": "step-54306",
        "selector": "#step-54306",
        "step_anchor": "step-2",
        "title": "Evaluating Expressions Where Multiplication Comes First",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Evaluate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5 \\times 4 -7.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Evaluate [MATH: 5 \\times 4 -7.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Multiplication should be carried out before addition or subtraction. We can emphasize this by using parentheses:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5 \\times 4 -7 = ({\\color{blue}5 \\times 4})-7]</span></p><p>We carry out the operations inside the parentheses first. We have</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{blue}5 \\times 4} = {\\color{blue}20}.]</span></p><p>Therefore,</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (5 \u00d7 4) \u2212 7|=; 20 \u2212 7|=; 13|.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Multiplication should be carried out before addition or subtraction. We can emphasize this by using parentheses:\n\n[MATH: 5 \\times 4 -7 = ({\\color{blue}5 \\times 4})-7]\n\nWe carry out the operations inside the parentheses first. We have\n\n[MATH: {\\color{blue}5 \\times 4} = {\\color{blue}20}.]\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: (5 \u00d7 4) \u2212 7|=; 20 \u2212 7|=; 13|.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: 5 \\times 4 -7.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nMultiplication should be carried out before addition or subtraction. We can emphasize this by using parentheses:\n\n[MATH: 5 \\times 4 -7 = ({\\color{blue}5 \\times 4})-7]\n\nWe carry out the operations inside the parentheses first. We have\n\n[MATH: {\\color{blue}5 \\times 4} = {\\color{blue}20}.]\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: (5 \u00d7 4) \u2212 7|=; 20 \u2212 7|=; 13|.]"
      },
