          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Multiplication should be carried out before addition or subtraction. We can emphasize this by using parentheses:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4+ 10 \\times 2 = 4 + ({\\color{blue}10 \\times 2})]</span></p><p>We carry out the operations inside the parentheses first. We have</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{blue}10 \\times 2} = {\\color{blue}20}.]</span></p><p>Therefore,</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4 + (10 \u00d7 2)|=; 4 + 20|=; 24|.]</span></p>",
