          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Multiplication should be carried out before addition or subtraction. We can emphasize this by using parentheses:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3 \\times 9 - 5 \\times 5 = ({\\color{blue}3 \\times 9}) - ({\\color{red}5 \\times 5})]</span></p><p>Now, we evaluate the products:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3 \u00d7 9|= 27; 5 \u00d7 5|= 25]</span></p><p>Therefore,</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (3 \u00d7 9) \u2212 (5 \u00d7 5)|=; 27 \u2212 25|=; 2|.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Multiplication should be carried out before addition or subtraction. We can emphasize this by using parentheses:\n\n[MATH: 3 \\times 9 - 5 \\times 5 = ({\\color{blue}3 \\times 9}) - ({\\color{red}5 \\times 5})]\n\nNow, we evaluate the products:\n\n[MATH: 3 \u00d7 9|= 27; 5 \u00d7 5|= 25]\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: (3 \u00d7 9) \u2212 (5 \u00d7 5)|=; 27 \u2212 25|=; 2|.]",
